    {
      "title": "Choosing Between Prompt, RAG and Fine-Tune",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Choosing Between Prompt, RAG and Fine-Tune",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Decision Order",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Prompt",
                    "sub": "+ few-shot baseline",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Add RAG",
                    "sub": "facts missing or stale",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Fine-tune",
                    "sub": "behavior still fails, or a smaller model is needed",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Compare",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Prompt",
                "RAG",
                "Fine-tune"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Data freshness",
                  "fixed",
                  "{green:best}",
                  "poor"
                ],
                [
                  "Style/format",
                  "ok",
                  "ok",
                  "{green:best}"
                ],
                [
                  "Setup effort",
                  "{green:lowest}",
                  "medium",
                  "highest"
                ],
                [
                  "Per-query cost",
                  "long prompts",
                  "adds context",
                  "can shrink prompts"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. When Each Wins",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Fine-tune wins",
                "RAG wins"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Strict output format",
                  "Data changes often"
                ],
                [
                  "Tone",
                  "Source citations needed"
                ],
                [
                  "High-volume classification or extraction",
                  "Per-user access control"
                ],
                [
                  "Replaces long few-shot, cuts tokens",
                  "Corpus too big for context"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Mistake",
              "text": "Fine-tuning to add fresh facts gives stale, hallucinated answers. Use ==RAG==."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Weekly policy changes?** ==RAG==: update the docs, no retraining; fine-tune only for tone",
                "**Fine-tune beat prompting?** Same held-out eval, prompt-only baseline vs tuned; compare metric, cost, latency",
                "**Long context replaces RAG?** Only for small corpora; cost, latency, no per-user access control or citations at scale"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Full Fine-Tuning vs LoRA and PEFT",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Full Fine-Tuning vs LoRA and PEFT",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Full FT vs PEFT",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Full FT== updates all weights",
                "Needs weights + gradients + Adam states: ~12-16 bytes/param",
                "==PEFT== freezes the base, trains few extra params"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. LoRA and QLoRA",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Method",
                "Trains",
                "7B memory"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Full FT",
                  "all weights",
                  "~100 GB+"
                ],
                [
                  "LoRA",
                  "BA, r 8-64, under 1%",
                  "far less"
                ],
                [
                  "QLoRA",
                  "LoRA on 4-bit base",
                  "one 16-24 GB GPU"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "LoRA: frozen W + trainable low-rank BA",
                "Adapters are ==MBs==, swappable per task or customer",
                "Merge into W: no extra latency",
                "Full FT: full model copy per task"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Key knobs",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Knob",
                "Setting"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "rank r",
                  "update capacity"
                ],
                [
                  "alpha",
                  "scaling, often 2r"
                ],
                [
                  "targets",
                  "attention q,v or all linear"
                ],
                [
                  "LR",
                  "LoRA 1e-4 to 2e-4, full FT ~1e-5"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "LR trap",
              "text": "Full-FT LR under-trains the adapter."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why low rank?** Updates have low intrinsic rank, so BA fits them",
                "**LoRA vs QLoRA?** QLoRA: less memory, small quality loss, slower",
                "**Full FT still worth it?** Big domain shift, new skills, top quality"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Data Needs, Costs and Distillation",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Data Needs, Costs and Distillation",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Data",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Quality== beats quantity",
                "Style/format with LoRA: ==100s–1000s== clean, diverse examples",
                "New skills or domains: {red:10k+} examples",
                "Instruction/response pairs or chat JSONL, same as the inference template",
                "Hold out ==10–20%== as eval set"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Cost",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Item",
                "Note"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Training",
                  "tokens × epochs × model size"
                ],
                [
                  "LoRA",
                  "mainly cuts memory; compute drops only modestly"
                ],
                [
                  "Hidden",
                  "labeling, eval, re-training per base upgrade"
                ],
                [
                  "Hosted fine-tune",
                  "often pricier per token than base"
                ],
                [
                  "Merged LoRA",
                  "self-hosted, no overhead"
                ],
                [
                  "Multi-adapter",
                  "one shared base"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Distillation",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Teacher",
                    "sub": "large model",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Student",
                    "sub": "small model",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Result",
                    "sub": "near-teacher quality, cheaper",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Teacher outputs: labels or soft logits",
                "Check teacher ==license terms==",
                "Best on a {orange:narrow task}"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**Examples needed?** Style: 100s–1000s; new skill: 10k+",
                "**Distill cost vs save?** Pay teacher once; save latency and serving cost",
                "**Safe synthetic data?** Dedupe, filter, keep a real eval set"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Eval set stays ==real==, never teacher-generated."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Choosing Model Size and Common Mistakes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Choosing Model Size and Common Mistakes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Size and Picking",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Per 1B params",
                "fp16",
                "4-bit"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Weights",
                  "~2 GB",
                  "~0.5 GB"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Strongest model",
                    "sub": "prove feasibility",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Step down",
                    "sub": "one size",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Eval check",
                    "sub": "metric vs target",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Keep last pass",
                    "sub": "smallest sufficient",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Bigger = ==better reasoning==, fewer failures; costs more {red:latency, cost, memory}",
                "Memory = weights + ==KV cache==",
                "Small **fine-tuned** model often beats a large prompted one on a narrow task"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Common Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Fine-tuning to add **knowledge**: hallucinated, stale facts; use ==RAG==",
                "No eval set or baseline: cannot tell if it helped",
                "Noisy, duplicated or ==test-leaking== data"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Over-training",
              "text": "Causes ==catastrophic forgetting== and overfitting. Fix: fewer epochs, lower LR, lower rank, mix in general data."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Smallest sufficient model?** Step down from the strongest until eval drops below target.",
                "**Catastrophic forgetting?** Tuning erases general skills; mix in general data.",
                "**Detect overfitting?** Train loss keeps falling while held-out eval worsens."
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
